# Task 11 Engine-Fidelity Observability — Final Handoff

## Outcome

COMPLETE. The engine now exposes the actual behavior-bearing strategy surface, binds it to fresh and resumed results, and provides aggregate-only point-in-time C/A provenance for the sealed Task 11 replay. This phase did not optimize the strategy, change trading decisions, select parameters, download data, regenerate a cache, or run a backtest.

CANSLIM is the strategy basis and initial policy family, not an immutable optimization objective. The effective policy assigns the later `maximize_return_and_minimize_drawdown` objective to the multi-agent backtest loop. Supported CANSLIM-derived thresholds, weights, gates, metric priorities, and portfolio/exit rules may be loosened or tightened there; PIT causality, next-session execution, source integrity, deterministic accounting, and truthful observability remain invariants.

